## Configuring Star-Tree Indexes in Pinot

Star-tree indexes are configured in the table configuration under the `tableIndexConfig` section using two settings [1][2]:

- **`starTreeIndexConfigs`** (list): Defines one or more star-tree index configurations
- **`enableDefaultStarTree`** (boolean): Enables or disables the default star-tree index

Here's the structure in your table config:

```json
{
  "tableIndexConfig": {
    "starTreeIndexConfigs": [
      {
        // Star-tree configuration details
      }
    ],
    "enableDefaultStarTree": true
  }
}
```

## Important Constraints

**Star-tree indexes are only applied to new segments.** Pinot does not support adding star-tree indexes to existing segments [1][2]. After you apply star-tree index configurations to the table configuration, only newly generated segments will have the star-tree indexes built.

Additionally, all star-tree dimension columns must be dictionary-encoded [5].

For detailed guidance on the specific fields within `starTreeIndexConfigs`, refer to the full star-tree index configuration documentation.

---

**Sources**

1. operate-pinot/troubleshooting/README.md — Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) > Indexing > Create star-tree indexes
2. operate-pinot/troubleshooting/ingestion-faq.md — Ingestion FAQ > Indexing > How to create star-tree indexes?
5. build-with-pinot/indexing/star-tree-index.md — Star-tree index > Limitations

